@Test

@BeforeMethod
@AfterMethod

@BeforeClass
@AfterClass

@BeforeTest
@AfterTest

@BeforeSuite
@AfterSuite

TC1
---
1.Login  -> @BeforeMethod
2.Search -> @Test
3.Logout -> @AfterMethod
4.Login  ->@Before
5.Adv Search -> @Test
6.Logout  ->@After

TC2
-------
1.Login  -> @BeforeClass
2.Search -> @Test
5.Adv Search -> @Test
6.Logout  ->AfterClass

Assertion -Validation point
---------------------------
2kinds of assertions
....................
1.Hard Assertions -> [In this Assert got failed, next lines will not execute]
                     [Hard assertion will be used last line in the class ]
                     [Hard Assert have static class, directly we can use.]

2.Soft Assertions -> [In this Assert got failed, next lines will execute]
                     [SoftAssert is not static class, we can create an object and use it]
                     [SoftAssert is always by-default is pass]
                     [At the end class use ->  "object name.assertAll()" ]
Note -> 1.Object is not directly create in the class.
        2.Object can create in main method and any method.
        3.SoftAssert is a class.
        4.Class object is created in main method and any method.
        5. "SoftAssert sa;" -> softassert is initiated in the class, then we can use in the any method in the class.

        Note ->
1.Conditional method -> will not failed,  if is not wrong.
2.Assert method -> will make fail, if is not wrong.
3.conditional with assert ->will make fail, if is not wrong.